---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import Layout from '~/layouts/Layout.astro'

import portrait from '~/assets/imgs/portrait.png'
import '~/styles/about.scss'
---

<Layout title='About Me'>
  <div class='cont'>
    <Image class={'portrait'} src={portrait} alt={'portrait'} height={720} quality={'max'} loading={'eager'} />
    <div class='txt'>
      <div class='top'>Hey, I'm <b>Lucas</b><span class='colonthree' /></div>
      <div style='margin:0;'>I'm a <span class='age'>21</span> year old animator, photographer, aviation nerd and typescript writer.</div>
      <div>
        I animate using <b><a href='https://blender.org' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'>Blender</a></b>,
        I've been using it for years now, but honestly, I don't think I'm <i>that</i> great at animating anyway.
        I was never taught animation and I don't yet fully even understand the funademental basics, I can't even animate a walk cycle.
      </div>
      <div>
        As for photography, the camera I use is the <b>Canon EOS R50</b>, and before that I used a <b>Panasonic Lumix DC-FZ82</b>.
        I was also never taught photography, so I'm entirely self-taught here too.
        I mostly just take pictures of planes that happen to fly over, but only really if they're military.<br>
        I take pictures of my dog when I walk her too, but my general focus is planes.
        I don't really go out to airports, I just take them from my back garden and hope they're close enough to get a good picture.
      </div>
      <div>
        To help with taking these pictures, I wrote some code that runs on my <b>Raspberry Pi 4</b>.
        The Pi sends a request to an API and fetches all planes within a 15 <i>nautical</i> mile radius of my location, it does this once every 30 seconds.<br>
        If the plane is military in the API's database it sends a notification to both my phone and my private Discord server detailing information like its type and operator.<br>
        I have a much more detailed explanation of it <a href='/projects/jetspotter'>here</a>.
      </div>
      <div>
        And as for filmmaking, although I've never been on a film set or been a part of anything huge,
        I <i>have</i> been to Pinewood Studios to help film for a documantary, so that's pretty cool!
        At the moment, I do volunteer at a local theatre that often does some filming of stuff, so that's pretty cool too.<br>
        Eventually, I would like to be able to actually be on film sets. Acting is never gonna be my thing but being able to do stuff behind the camera would be great.
        Something I've always wanted to do is be the guy who records "B-Roll" for behind the scenes videos and such,
        especially if I get to record stuff like in <a href='https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OwDfxYDSeDU' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'>this video for <b>The Grand Budapest Hotel</b></a> or <a href='https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5OGWPtaUOok' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'>this video for <b>The Adventures of Tintin</b></a>.
      </div>
      <div>As for web stuff, I typically write Typescript/Javascript for backend stuff and I usually use <a href='https://astro.build' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'>Astro</a> or <a href='https://expressjs.com' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'>Express</a> for frontend.</div>
      <div>
        Ssome of my favourite music artists are <b><a href='https://www.last.fm/music/Kiltro' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'>Kiltro</a></b>, <b><a href='https://www.last.fm/music/Crosa+Rosa' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'>Crosa Rosa</a></b> and <b><a href='https://www.last.fm/music/Blood+Cultures' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'>Blood Cultures</a></b>.<br>
        I listen to <b>a lot</b> of different genres, spanning from <b>Kiltro</b> who do Chilean folk, to <b>Crosa Rosa</b> who do psychedelic rock, to <b>The Correspondents</b> who do electro swing and then all the way to <b>Maria Asahina</b> who does J-Pop.
      </div>
      <div>
        And finally, I'd thought I'd mention that <i>yes</i> I am a furry if it weren't blatantly obvious.
        I don't even know how long I've been a furry for but at least since 2018 <i>(or that's what the date on my oldest ref sheet tells me)</i>.<br>
        But I much prefer to be called by my IRL name rather than my sona's name.
        I'm not entirely sure why, I still use the full <b>InvisyArcticFox</b> username for all social media I'm on,
        but if I can, I'll always set my display name to my IRL name.
        I guess I could always rename my sona to have the same first name, but it honestly doesn't have a good ring to it,
        and I'd also have to update my username <i>everywhere</i>.<br>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script src='../scripts/colonthree.ts' />
<script src='../scripts/age.ts' />